# Copy to .env (Bun auto-loads it). Never commit real secrets.

# Headless auth via email/password (for accounts that allow password login). If set and no session
# exists, the server logs in on startup — and re-logs in automatically when the session expires
# (self-healing). MFA optional.
# FORKABLE_EMAIL=
# FORKABLE_PASSWORD=
# FORKABLE_MFA=

# Headless auth via a full forkable.com Cookie header ("_easyorder_session=…; AWSALBTG=…; …"). Use
# this for SSO-only accounts. Provisioned on startup if set; CSRF is minted automatically (pin one
# with FORKABLE_CSRF only if you need to).
# FORKABLE_COOKIE=
# FORKABLE_CSRF=

# Optional: override the HMAC key for write confirm-tokens. If unset, a per-install key is
# generated and stored in the session file. Set this to pin it across machines.
# FORKABLE_WRITE_SECRET=

# Optional: override the session store location (default ~/.forkable-mcp/session.json).
# FORKABLE_MCP_HOME=
